d worked once; perhaps it was time to try it again.</p>\n\n<p>4 But his neighbors still scoffed. What did Sawadogo know?</p>\n\n<p>5 To the amazement of many, Sawadogo was right. Today his patch of green forest grows in the midst of a desert. Slowly over the years, many of those who laughed at their neighbor have now joined him. More and more fields in West Africa are being rescued from desertification using Sawadogo’s zaï and other water harvesting processes. Sawadogo travels all over the region and spreads the message of how zaï farming can transform the landscape and save lives. He knows there is hope for a brighter future.</p>\n\n<p><u><em><strong>Use “A Legacy of Stone” and “Trees Rise in the Desert” to answer question 14.</strong></em></u></p>\n\n<p>14.&nbsp;<strong>Both</strong> the author of the selection “A Legacy of Stone” and the author of the selection “Trees Rise in the Desert” would most likely agree with which statement?</p>\n","ui_style":{"type":"horizontal","choice_label":"upper-alpha"},"response_id":"8af17232-7191-5ee0-92b5-e67027243641_51bd668e5231fd284f16bb0ee9e9f263"},"response":{"value":["0"],"type":"array","apiVersion":"v2.197.15","revision":1},"creation_date":"2024-04-04 18:13:48","mod_date":"2024-04-04 18:21:38","persist_until":"2027-04-04 18:13:48","saved":true},{"id":"0157_luser-5105cf1f-0de6-5c6b-b31b-574b2b3e2460_8af17232-7191-5ee0-92b5-e67027243641_3afcd7ac963cab026a676c5c4726dcf8","user_id":"luser-5105cf1f-0de6-5c6b-b31b-574b2b3e2460","response_id":"8af17232-7191-5ee0-92b5-e67027243641_3afcd7ac963cab026a676c5c4726dcf8","type":"mcq","question":{"type":"mcq","options":[{"label":"Forty-three-year-old Cheval continued collecting stones along his route for almost 20 years. (paragraph 4)","value":"0"},{"label":"At night he labored by the light of an oil lamp. (paragraph 5)","value":"1"},{"label":"But as his palace took shape, people’s criticisms were replaced by awed respect. (paragraph 6)","value":"2"},{"label":"Cheval’s uniqueness helped h